WEBVTT

00:04.050 --> 00:05.770
I'm taking some time off.

00:05.770 --> 00:06.600
What?

00:06.600 --> 00:08.420
Someone in my family 
seems to have collapsed.

00:08.930 --> 00:10.250
Your family?

00:11.340 --> 00:14.260
Stop asking questions and 
head to the airport.

02:02.480 --> 02:03.440
Hey.

02:03.800 --> 02:04.600
Hey.

02:05.180 --> 02:06.640
How's Lucy?

02:09.340 --> 02:11.720
She's been out for a whole ten days now.

02:12.560 --> 02:13.400
Yeah.

02:13.870 --> 02:15.450
Are <i>you</i> okay, Chise?

02:15.780 --> 02:17.800
You've been with her this 
whole time, right?

02:17.800 --> 02:19.780
I'm fine.

02:20.350 --> 02:25.480
<i>I guess I shouldn't tell him yet that 
I have enough magic power to spare.</i>

02:27.700 --> 02:29.910
Zoe, are you here?

02:29.910 --> 02:31.210
Yes.

02:31.840 --> 02:33.050
Gotta go.

02:33.050 --> 02:34.620
Your routine physical?

02:34.620 --> 02:35.450
Yeah.

02:35.450 --> 02:36.860
Don't push yourself too much.

02:37.210 --> 02:38.300
Thanks.

02:46.260 --> 02:47.860
I hope she's okay.

02:48.280 --> 02:50.150
You say that every day.

02:55.680 --> 02:57.410
I'm worried.

02:57.850 --> 03:01.250
We still don't know why she lost 
her magic power all of a sudden.

03:02.940 --> 03:06.490
Hey, what is it like to feel "worried"?

03:07.030 --> 03:10.470
Your head and guts feel agitated.

03:10.470 --> 03:13.140
You keep thinking about a nasty future.

03:13.640 --> 03:14.740
And...

03:15.850 --> 03:16.850
It's scary?

03:17.300 --> 03:19.640
That's part of it, too.

03:19.640 --> 03:20.520
Ah.

03:21.020 --> 03:25.310
So like the time I couldn't focus on 
anything while you were unconscious.

03:27.590 --> 03:29.430
Does what's happening to her bother you?

03:29.430 --> 03:32.470
Well, it does worry me.

03:36.500 --> 03:37.840
Elias...

03:37.840 --> 03:38.870
What is it?

03:38.870 --> 03:42.100
You and Lucy don't have the same role.

03:42.100 --> 03:43.990
I know, I know.

03:44.420 --> 03:46.420
I hope you know, too.

03:46.890 --> 03:51.120
I'm confident I'm the one who 
worries for you the most.

03:51.560 --> 03:55.320
My guts cooled back down when you came back.

03:57.150 --> 03:58.840
What happened to your hair?

03:58.840 --> 04:00.370
I'm home.

04:00.370 --> 04:01.650
Welcome home.

04:01.650 --> 04:03.570
What happened to your hair?

04:03.570 --> 04:05.630
He can fill you in.

04:06.230 --> 04:08.080
I'm home, me.

04:08.080 --> 04:09.530
Welcome home, me.

04:14.690 --> 04:17.800
You sure do put yourself in danger.

04:17.800 --> 04:19.690
I can't look away for even a second.

04:19.970 --> 04:22.980
I couldn't have done anything 
different this time.

04:22.980 --> 04:24.160
Well...

04:24.160 --> 04:25.690
Yes, you're right.

04:26.070 --> 04:30.960
Still, your first thought shouldn't have 
been to go look for her by yourself.

04:31.380 --> 04:32.530
Right...

04:34.160 --> 04:39.700
Though, as a mage, it wasn't a bad decision.

04:40.300 --> 04:42.720
Th-Thank you.

04:43.600 --> 04:44.840
Also...

04:45.510 --> 04:49.150
The way you went about it was 
something I would have done.

04:49.590 --> 04:53.330
I don't really get it, either.

04:53.900 --> 04:59.110
It felt like I could hear someone's 
voice from somewhere deep.

05:07.770 --> 05:11.800
And that's why you came to me?

05:12.800 --> 05:14.450
Good night.

05:17.190 --> 05:21.510
You're the only one who's been 
inside me for a long time.

05:21.860 --> 05:26.170
Why am I the one person 
you're so flippant with?

05:27.320 --> 05:31.140
So, what do you think that voice is?

05:37.500 --> 05:38.980
Something bad.

05:42.780 --> 05:46.660
It tried to stop something from killing you.

05:47.450 --> 05:48.610
Is that evil?

05:49.900 --> 05:52.620
I don't think I should have gone so far.

05:53.440 --> 05:57.180
But that was all I could do, it said.

05:57.970 --> 06:00.400
You're only here to regret 
it because you survived.

06:02.670 --> 06:07.740
Though, I can't imagine you would have 
died so easily, given who you are now.

06:08.120 --> 06:11.220
Was that the voice of the dragon?

06:11.220 --> 06:12.130
Or...

06:12.130 --> 06:13.320
Dunno.

06:13.700 --> 06:15.110
One thing's certain...

06:16.660 --> 06:20.270
The voice came from within you.

06:26.710 --> 06:28.380
I'm sleepy.

06:28.380 --> 06:29.350
Go.

06:32.620 --> 06:33.630
Thanks.

06:42.470 --> 06:47.910
<i>You heard the voice of a dragon 
gone mad, having cursed a human.</i>

06:49.280 --> 06:51.710
<i>You've had a taste of my past.</i>

06:52.700 --> 06:55.420
<i>You saw the source of malice and animus.</i>

06:57.640 --> 07:02.190
<i>Guided by the voice, you 
learned to hurt another.</i>

07:03.530 --> 07:06.710
<i>Once you know you can bare 
your fangs at your enemy,</i>

07:08.830 --> 07:13.720
<i>there's no going back to when
 you didn't know anything.</i>

07:16.110 --> 07:18.910
You went to ask Cartaphilus?

07:19.690 --> 07:22.300
Even though I'm your master?

07:22.300 --> 07:23.130
I mean...

07:23.130 --> 07:25.350
I thought it'd be best to ask 
someone who knows what it's like.

07:25.810 --> 07:27.010
Hello.

07:33.270 --> 07:34.520
Seth-san.

07:34.520 --> 07:36.060
Well, well, Chise.

07:36.590 --> 07:38.210
Why are you here?

07:38.210 --> 07:40.910
I'm at the College right now.

07:40.910 --> 07:42.670
Why are you here?

07:43.250 --> 07:45.790
I was told that a family member collapsed.

07:45.790 --> 07:47.930
Seth Noel, correct?

07:48.360 --> 07:52.270
I believe I contacted you the day
 after the practical, did I not?

07:52.610 --> 07:55.820
I was busy with work. I apologize.

07:55.820 --> 07:57.940
How is my sister, Lucy?

07:58.720 --> 08:00.850
She hasn't woken up yet.

08:01.270 --> 08:04.270
Huh, you're Lucy's brother?

08:04.270 --> 08:06.320
Oh, are you acquainted?

08:06.730 --> 08:08.340
She's my roommate.

08:08.340 --> 08:09.760
What a surprise.

08:10.360 --> 08:12.560
I'd like to explain Lucy's condition.

08:13.010 --> 08:14.310
Please come this sway.

08:15.060 --> 08:19.240
She's a difficult person, but I hope 
you can give her your friendship.

08:26.150 --> 08:28.140
They were siblings...

08:33.620 --> 08:34.710
Lucy!

09:06.230 --> 09:07.220
Give them back!

09:08.180 --> 09:11.400
Give us back our spiders!

09:21.400 --> 09:22.540
Chise.

09:23.550 --> 09:24.660
Lucy!

09:24.940 --> 09:26.320
You're awake!

09:30.230 --> 09:32.930
Wh-Why are you here?

09:33.370 --> 09:36.380
I got word that you'd 
collapsed while in a practical.

09:36.820 --> 09:39.170
You were out for ten days.

09:39.740 --> 09:40.990
Ten days?

09:42.490 --> 09:43.630
Go away!

09:44.320 --> 09:45.730
Go away!

09:45.000 --> 09:46.760
You need to be in bed!

09:45.730 --> 09:46.760
Leave!

09:47.420 --> 09:50.650
I don't want a loser like 
you to worry for me!

09:51.000 --> 09:53.270
Just get lost!

09:53.270 --> 09:54.530
Lucy!

09:59.490 --> 10:01.370
I'll stay by her side for a while.

10:01.700 --> 10:03.780
She seems to still be unstable.

10:17.220 --> 10:19.380
<i>What was that?</i>

10:22.130 --> 10:24.300
<i>I smell orange and lavender...</i>

10:24.740 --> 10:25.880
Philomela?

10:38.630 --> 10:40.500
Were you practicing?

10:40.880 --> 10:42.530
Y-Yeah.

10:43.200 --> 10:45.070
S-Sorry.

10:45.070 --> 10:47.010
I didn't mean to interrupt.

10:49.040 --> 10:52.910
It seems like you're still 
holding onto that potpourri.

10:52.910 --> 10:54.000
How was the tea?

10:54.000 --> 10:55.220
Was it all right?

10:55.890 --> 10:57.270
It was fine.

10:57.660 --> 11:01.080
I hope you'll let me know if you run out.

11:01.080 --> 11:02.550
I'll make some more.

11:05.900 --> 11:09.130
Why do you do so much for me?

11:10.020 --> 11:11.680
I don't know.

11:11.680 --> 11:12.740
Sorry.

11:12.740 --> 11:13.650
I...

11:14.160 --> 11:16.870
I just felt an urge to talk to you.

11:17.570 --> 11:18.280
Er...

11:18.280 --> 11:20.920
I'll stop if it's bothering you.

11:27.890 --> 11:28.820
Umm...

11:29.600 --> 11:33.050
I'm not used to talking 
in front of other people.

11:34.520 --> 11:39.300
I don't mind when it's just the two of us.

11:40.540 --> 11:41.540
Got it.

11:41.890 --> 11:43.550
Okay, bye.

11:47.020 --> 11:47.890
Chise.

11:48.360 --> 11:49.290
Isaac.

11:49.290 --> 11:49.810
Rian.

11:51.180 --> 11:52.240
<i>I see.</i>

11:52.240 --> 11:53.440
<i>Because the boys showed up.</i>

11:55.160 --> 11:56.290
How's Lucy?

11:56.650 --> 12:00.000
She just woke up, but then she passed out again.

12:00.400 --> 12:01.380
I see.

12:01.380 --> 12:02.230
That's a relief.

12:03.090 --> 12:04.740
Explain!

12:04.990 --> 12:08.920
Are there any records of something being 
taken from the Forbidden Books Storage?!

12:09.220 --> 12:10.950
Has it been used in an experiment?!

12:11.310 --> 12:13.680
Not when we did our routine check.

12:14.480 --> 12:16.730
Then why has it fallen apart?!

12:17.640 --> 12:18.950
No...

12:19.330 --> 12:22.050
Has it been replaced with a fake?!

12:39.200 --> 12:42.820
Instructors, I thank you for coming.

12:43.400 --> 12:46.400
There's been a bit of an emergency.

12:47.370 --> 12:50.830
Upon inspections of the 
Forbidden Books Storage today,

12:50.830 --> 12:54.810
the book in Storage Number 5 
was found to have crumbled.

12:54.810 --> 12:55.840
A forbidden book?

12:55.840 --> 12:57.760
Even though it was in storage?

12:58.440 --> 13:03.640
Upon investigation, we've determined that 
the book that had crumbed was a fake.

13:06.890 --> 13:12.250
So that book was a fake 
the entire time it was in storage?

13:12.250 --> 13:15.020
Or was it swapped out recently?

13:15.200 --> 13:18.790
We believe it was swapped out 
in the past several days.

13:18.790 --> 13:20.910
What is the nature of the book?

13:20.910 --> 13:21.890
What is it called?

13:21.890 --> 13:23.510
Is it dangerous?

13:23.510 --> 13:26.290
Is it an original manuscript or a copy?

13:26.290 --> 13:28.170
Let's see...

13:28.980 --> 13:32.360
It's a book called<i> The 
Testament of Carnamagos</i>.

13:35.990 --> 13:38.470
Wasn't that the book you...

13:38.810 --> 13:42.960
It's said that simply reading 
it can affect the reader.

13:42.960 --> 13:46.430
We librarians don't know much 
about its contents ourselves.

13:46.730 --> 13:50.180
The book stored in the library 
in England is a copy,

13:50.180 --> 13:53.430
and we suspect it won't have as 
much of an effect as the original.

13:53.630 --> 13:58.220
But to be honest, we have no idea how 
much of an effect that would be.

13:58.830 --> 14:02.150
I've read that book before.

14:02.150 --> 14:04.120
<i>Wait, wait, wait!</i>

14:04.390 --> 14:05.610
And its contents?

14:05.870 --> 14:08.560
I'd borrowed it from an acquaintance.

14:09.240 --> 14:15.520
It offered a few insights, but I gave the 
book back before I could make use of it.

14:15.910 --> 14:18.370
<i>Well, he's not </i>lying<i>.</i>

14:18.370 --> 14:22.580
Would it be possible for you to describe 
it to an extent that won't affect us?

14:27.790 --> 14:31.880
It can put the living in 
mortal danger at times.

14:34.750 --> 14:39.580
It describes ways to take in the life 
force and magic power of others.

14:39.580 --> 14:41.350
How to create immortals.

14:41.350 --> 14:43.570
How to destroy them.

14:44.060 --> 14:46.860
How to bring back the dead.

14:47.310 --> 14:48.550
I see.

14:48.970 --> 14:51.170
That does sound like something 
that would be forbidden.

14:52.130 --> 14:55.130
Why did you choose to read it?

14:55.390 --> 14:57.600
It was intriguing.

14:58.170 --> 15:01.160
But it turned out that
 I don't have a use for it.

15:01.550 --> 15:05.670
Reading it comes at a 
great cost for a person.

15:06.330 --> 15:11.930
<i>I guess he's putting it out in the open 
so there's no reason to suspect him.</i>

15:12.450 --> 15:14.510
Thank you very much.

15:14.510 --> 15:16.050
That was very informative.

15:16.700 --> 15:20.890
We will continue investigations 
both internally and more broadly.

15:21.260 --> 15:25.410
Please let us know if you learn of anything.

15:25.820 --> 15:32.370
Given that it can affect humans, 
it could cause an incident.

15:32.780 --> 15:35.570
In that event, we'll be calling 
upon you for cooperation.

15:36.010 --> 15:37.730
Keep that in mind.

15:38.070 --> 15:39.420
Yes, ma'am.

15:39.420 --> 15:40.230
Please!

15:40.230 --> 15:42.470
This isn't the time to remind 
us that you're free spirits.

15:42.470 --> 15:43.830
We need you to be serious.

15:43.830 --> 15:46.670
I'm sorry, there's one more thing...

15:46.670 --> 15:49.050
About the remains of the book...

15:49.540 --> 15:55.670
There's a special spider silk woven into the 
cover and several other parts of the book.

15:55.670 --> 15:57.020
Spider silk?

15:58.540 --> 15:59.760
Could it be...

15:59.760 --> 16:01.510
Is that the Webster family's silk?

16:05.230 --> 16:07.400
It's possible.

16:07.900 --> 16:11.850
Please take care that this information 
does not land on the ears

16:11.850 --> 16:15.080
of our student, Lucy Webster.

16:17.250 --> 16:18.360
Well...

16:18.750 --> 16:21.330
Please remember to be careful.

16:22.120 --> 16:25.390
And please don't get too 
lost in your research.

16:31.340 --> 16:33.800
What's this about the 
Webster's family spiders?

16:34.270 --> 16:36.490
Oh, right.

16:36.490 --> 16:39.260
You're a mage, so you wouldn't know.

16:39.930 --> 16:40.970
Webster is...

16:40.970 --> 16:42.360
Mr. Ainsworth.

16:50.850 --> 16:52.290
Nice to meet you.

16:52.290 --> 16:54.480
I'm Simeon Paladilhe.

16:54.480 --> 16:57.790
I'd heard a mage was here, 
so I've been eager to meet you.

16:57.790 --> 16:59.850
Ah, so <i>you're</i> the mage!

16:59.850 --> 17:00.610
Huh.

17:00.610 --> 17:02.710
I hear you're using a magic disguise!

17:02.710 --> 17:05.700
That's impressive. I would
 have never known.

17:05.700 --> 17:08.380
Mages can transform, too?

17:10.410 --> 17:11.270
He's bone!

17:11.270 --> 17:12.850
A dog? A wolf?

17:12.850 --> 17:14.180
Do you swallow your food whole?

17:14.450 --> 17:16.770
Come on! He was in the middle of a question!

17:17.130 --> 17:18.360
A question?

17:18.920 --> 17:22.940
He doesn't know about the Webster tragedy.

17:29.580 --> 17:31.370
The Webster tragedy...

17:32.310 --> 17:35.670
Around here, it could 
have happened to anyone.

17:36.450 --> 17:41.710
The Webster family made a living by 
producing and duplicating magic books.

17:42.300 --> 17:47.500
Their books were famous for 
being just like the original.

17:47.920 --> 17:51.960
They were also famous for 
the spiders that they kept.

17:52.320 --> 17:53.250
Spiders?

17:54.000 --> 17:57.380
The pages were made in part using 
the silk that the spiders spun.

17:57.380 --> 18:00.430
And they were bound using the silk, too.

18:02.230 --> 18:04.760
They never revealed much of the details.

18:04.760 --> 18:06.440
It's just what was surmised.

18:06.910 --> 18:13.460
And eight years ago, the entire Webster 
family, excluding one person, was murdered.

18:13.820 --> 18:15.980
We don't know who did it.

18:16.440 --> 18:20.220
The survivor is a student at the College.

18:20.220 --> 18:22.840
But their spiders were all stolen.

18:24.260 --> 18:26.870
There are rumors about a spy being involved.

18:26.870 --> 18:28.900
Though that's not certain, either.

18:29.870 --> 18:35.530
The eldest son, who was slated to inherit 
the business, had no control of magic.

18:35.530 --> 18:37.740
He'd been driven out of the family.

18:38.150 --> 18:39.590
Ah.

18:43.510 --> 18:48.530
Plenty of people know about the incident, 
but it's just, y'know... a lot.

18:48.920 --> 18:51.310
It's better not to talk about it too much.

18:51.790 --> 18:52.930
Understood.

18:54.630 --> 18:55.640
Thanks.

18:57.720 --> 18:59.350
You're welcome.

18:59.350 --> 19:00.610
He's a proper person.

19:00.610 --> 19:02.400
He's proper enough to say thanks.

19:02.970 --> 19:04.270
Well, we'll see you.

19:07.910 --> 19:12.670
The people here don't seem to 
be bothered by the likes of me.

19:13.120 --> 19:14.580
Your appearance, you mean?

19:14.580 --> 19:15.630
It's hard to ignore.

19:15.630 --> 19:19.460
There are still plenty of people 
who will talk behind your back.

19:19.460 --> 19:22.060
But here, it's perfectly normal.

19:22.060 --> 19:24.350
So long as you do your work, 
people will support you.

19:24.970 --> 19:28.590
I'm sure you'll like life here.

19:31.160 --> 19:32.070
Later.

19:35.510 --> 19:38.150
That's Simeon Paladilhe.

19:38.150 --> 19:40.170
He's studying sound sorcery.

19:40.540 --> 19:42.590
He's pretty easy to talk to, huh?

19:43.020 --> 19:43.810
Hm?

19:45.130 --> 19:48.020
Why don't you try befriending him?

19:48.680 --> 19:50.000
Friend?

19:50.780 --> 19:53.910
Chise talks about her friends quite often.

19:54.710 --> 19:58.090
I don't really understand friendships.

19:58.090 --> 20:00.270
Are they different from acquaintances?

20:00.270 --> 20:02.840
Acquaintances are just acquaintances.

20:02.840 --> 20:05.100
Friends are more special.

20:05.570 --> 20:08.180
Not that I have all that many.

20:08.690 --> 20:09.310
Oh!

20:09.790 --> 20:13.370
Why don't we become friends 
from now on, then?

20:17.570 --> 20:19.470
With you, I'll pass.

21:10.210 --> 21:11.730
<i>He has bags under his eyes.</i>

21:18.180 --> 21:19.480
<i>What a dumbass.</i>

21:20.000 --> 21:23.320
<i>I know you hate me.</i>

21:32.060 --> 21:35.510
<i>He said he'd be fine without 
security in the College.</i>

21:35.510 --> 21:37.380
<i>I'm not so sure, though...</i>

21:38.060 --> 21:40.260
Shoot, need smokes.

22:15.980 --> 22:18.040
The guard has been picked off.

22:18.490 --> 22:23.460
Let's clean this up and finish the pickup.
